'''Abiphones''', short for '''Ability Phones'''<ref>See [[Alwin#Dialogue|Alwin's dialogue]].</ref>, are items that allow the player to call [[NPC]]s remotely without having to interact with them physically. 

== Obtaining ==
{{NPCSprite|Alda}} sells the '''Abiphone Basic''' at {{Zone|Abiphones & Co.}} in the [[Hub]]. All other Abiphones can be purchased from {{NPCSprite|Udel}} or {{NPCSprite|Nuvian}} in the {{Zone|Crimson Isle}}.

== Abiphones ==
{{/Table}}

== Usage ==
=== Contacts ===
Certain [[NPCs]] have contacts, and the player can obtain them by completing quests given by the [[NPC]]. To obtain '''Abiphone''' dialogue, the player must {{Gold|right-click}} the desired [[NPC]] with an '''Abiphone''' in hand. Each unique contact grants {{SkyBlock XP|+10}}. This can only be completed once per contact.
*'''Abiphone Contacts''' cannot be obtained from [[Visitors]] on the [[Garden]] and instead must be obtained normally.
{{/ContactsTable}}

=== Contact Slots ===
An extra {{Aqua|+3}} contact slots can be obtained from using a {{Item|Abiphone Contacts Trio}}. This can be used up to {{Red|25}} times, granting a total of {{Aqua|+75}} contact slots, and is added on top of the current model's contact limit.

An extra {{Aqua|+1}} contact slot can be achieved from the {{ID|Sumsung© G3 Abicase}}, or an extra {{Aqua|+2}} contact slots from the {{ID|Sumsung© GG Abicase}}.

Up to {{DarkPurple|+2}} extra contact slots can be achieved from completing [[9f™ Network]] relays.

=== Extra Features ===
Some '''Abiphones''' that have a high enough model have extra features. '''{{Pink|Tic Tac Toe}}''' and '''{{Pink|Snake}}''' are games that can be played through an interface, whilst the '''{{Green|Contact Directory}}''' allows players to view the full list of contacts, see which ones they are missing and organize the list alphabetically.

